        "original_id": "2cabab81-c4ef-58ea-926c-55b2a9f79021",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Fancy Free, “Elvira”, Ain't Living Long Like This, “An American Dream”, “Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down”, “(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I”, “Voilá, An American Dream”\n- People: The Oak Ridge Boys, Dallas Frazier\n\nFacts:\n- In 1978, “Voilá, An American Dream” was recorded for the album Ain't Living Long Like This and was released as the B-side of the single “(Now and Then There's) A Fool Such as I”.\n- On March 26, 1981, The Oak Ridge Boys released Fancy Free as their fifth country studio album.\n- In 1981, Dallas Frazier’s song “Elvira” became a country and pop hit for The Oak Ridge Boys and is considered one of their signature songs.\n- The songs “Elvira”, “Baby Better Start Turnin' 'Em Down”, and “(Now and Then, There's) A Fool Such as I” were released as singles, but none reached the top 40.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
